{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /workspace/proposal.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"parent_trial\\\": \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n  \\\"study\\\": {\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"g1-capacity-storage-interaction-factorial\\\",\n    \\\"protocol_ref\\\": \\\"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\\\",\n    \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"baseline-din\\\", \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-dense_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"],\n    \\\"question\\\": \\\"Does the loss from uniform width reduction arise primarily from embedding-table rank/storage, from the dimension presented to the nonlinear scorer and towers, or from their interaction? Can an 8-dimensional table with a learned lift to 16 interaction coordinates retain the stronger source click AUC with fewer parameters and lower measured prediction cost?\\\",\n    \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Observed limitation: uniform E8 simultaneously reduced table width, target/history/context coordinates, the coordinate-product interaction and tower input widths. It saved about half the parameters but lost 0.00286509 click AUC. Dense-half lost 0.00117365 AUC with little parameter saving; applying dense-half at E8 instead increased AUC by 0.00041215 relative to embedding_half, an exploratory interaction of +0.00158580. These single-seed results do not locate redundant capacity. Provisional mechanism: some of the E8 loss may reflect the restricted geometry and input capacity of the nonlinear interaction rather than table rank alone. Separate raw table width R from downstream field width D through learned bias-free field projections, and test all four R,D in {8,16}. An R8,D16 lift remains rank at most eight per table; it cannot recreate an unrestricted 16-dimensional lookup. Its possible benefit is a learned interaction basis and wider nonlinear readout, not restored information. This is a diagnostic hypothesis, not demonstrated redundancy or a new-architecture claim.\\\",\n    \\\"nearest_work\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"trial://g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"implementation_checked\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Closest executable architecture: action-aware unnormalized DIN scorer over 30 masked uniform/feedback block summaries, four towers, auxiliary scorer/item gradient blocking with context gradients retained. Preserve all these operators and hidden widths; add a shared-by-table bias-free projection to decouple stored width from interaction width. Existing g1-r0006 factorial varied uniform embedding width and hidden widths, whereas this factorial holds hidden widths fixed and separates table width from downstream input width.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"paper:din\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"read\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Archived exact-version primary text inspected at lines 175-274: field embedding concatenation, target-dependent local activation, explicit product interactions and unnormalized pooling are inherited ideas. The local source adds block compression, four tasks and path gates. This proposal studies table/interaction width separation inside that source; no exact original DIN reproduction or novelty is claimed.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/embeddings/feature_embedding.py\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"implementation_checked\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Pinned implementation inspected at lines 55-200. Retain FeatureEmbeddingDict and its lookup sharing, padding and registered nn.Embedding modules. Add learned dense field projections after embedding/compression. Alias projections when their actual embedding modules are identical. Do not modify the host FeatureMap or vocabularies. Reject unexpected field dimension overrides/encoders rather than silently changing information.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"unirank-benchmark-v2\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"read\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Primary benchmark section 2.3 describes Zenith's separate ID paths, EST's cross-attention/feature-specific FFNs and SSR's sparse competitive filtering. None of these architectures is implemented here. The change is uniform table-to-interaction projection under an unchanged compressed source. Benchmark descriptions are not original-method full-paper audits.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"paper:zenith\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"discovered\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Authorized record provides a primary-paper link and provenance only, with content_read=false. No original-method mechanism verification or priority comparison is asserted. The authorized paper search did not furnish an audited primary source for factorized recommendation embeddings; broader nearest-work coverage and originality remain unverified.\\\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"inherited_components\\\": [\n      \\\"Frozen data identity, official_offline visibility, four labels, supplied context/item/action fields, 100-event masks and temporal split.\\\",\n      \\\"g2-r0004-context_only source and its exact 10 blocks x 3 masked mean summaries, count weighting and uniform-click/feedback-auxiliary routing.\\\",\n      \\\"Action-aware unnormalized shared local activation with Dice and hidden widths 64/32; four separate towers with hidden widths 128/64.\\\",\n      \\\"Auxiliary functional scorer with detached parameters and cloned Dice buffers; item/action path detached for auxiliaries; context path trainable; single scorer call during inference.\\\",\n      \\\"Default sum of four unweighted BCEs; frozen single-pass host recipe, seed, optimizers, batch size, precision and scorers. No training-loss hook.\\\",\n      \\\"Framework embedding lookup and shared target/history tables, with all source fields retained.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"proposed_difference\\\": \\\"Four standalone cells independently set raw table width R and downstream per-field width D to 8 or 16. Every cell, including both square controls, adds one trainable bias-free R-to-D field map per unique underlying embedding module. Projections are initialized with orthogonal weights and gain sqrt(max(1,D/R)), after the source reset; this preserves average output-coordinate variance only for isotropic independent inputs. Raw histories are compressed before projection; linearity makes this equivalent in exact arithmetic to projecting each history before masked averaging. Current target and context use the same per-field maps; target/history aliases remain tied. Hidden scorer/tower widths and source gradient gates are unchanged. R8,D16 is the primary candidate; R16,D8 is a diagnostic replacement candidate, not expected to halve storage. R8,D8 and R16,D16 control for the added projection operator. Each module supplies a literal CONFIG and Model with the frozen prediction API. No new forward inputs, field removal, loss weights, data passes or optimizer changes.\\\",\n    \\\"predictions\\\": [\n      \\\"Primary diagnostic: if nonlinear interaction width matters beyond table rank, AUC(table8_interact16) exceeds AUC(table8_interact8), with a smaller gap between table8_interact16 and table16_interact16 than between the two square cells. Compare the difference of D effects across R to measure interaction, without presuming its sign.\\\",\n      \\\"If raw table rank is the dominant limitation, table8_interact16 remains below table16_interact16 despite identical downstream input and hidden widths. If compact downstream geometry is sufficient, table16_interact8 retains AUC relative to table16_interact16, isolating a possible latency reduction without a large storage benefit.\\\",\n      \\\"Operational screening retention is click AUC at least 0.660146940486458 (source 0.660646940486458 minus a predeclared 0.0005 margin), total parameters at least 40% below 32060453, and both model-only p50/p95 latency at least 5% below source replay 11.77057/11.90825 ms. Report whole-validation throughput separately; prefer a concurrent host timing control if authorized. These screening thresholds are not a confidence interval or established noninferiority. A joint efficiency claim needs repeated quality and timing support.\\\",\n      \\\"Embedding parameters should equal 15896608 at R8 or 31793216 at R16 if the original sharing/schema audit passes. With K unique projection owners, total counts should be 16048645+64K (R8,D8), 16163845+128K (R8,D16), 31945253+128K (R16,D8), and 32060453+256K (R16,D16). K and actual counts must be measured by the host. These are storage arithmetic predictions, not latency predictions.\\\",\n      \\\"Report all four AUC/logloss pairs, auxiliary mean separately, train/allocated-GPU/wall seconds, examples processed, peak memory, parameter split, validation inference seconds, throughput and p50/p95 batch latency. Source cart/fav/buy AUCs already trail baseline-din substantially; retaining click AUC must never be reported as retaining all-task quality. Use only existing history-length slice rules and show positives/negatives; slices and cross-cell effects remain exploratory until repeated.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"falsifiers\\\": [\n      \\\"No advantage of R8,D16 over R8,D8, together with a persistent gap to R16,D16, rejects the tested interaction-width rescue; it does not refute every mixed-width or low-rank design.\\\",\n      \\\"Neither R8 cell reaches the predeclared source-retention margin, or retention fails in later paired repetitions: no supported claim of preserving the stronger source at half table storage.\\\",\n      \\\"A compact-table cell that retains AUC but does not improve measured latency/throughput fails the joint prediction-cost claim. Parameter savings or FLOP estimates alone are insufficient.\\\",\n      \\\"If R16,D16 materially shifts quality relative to g1-r0006-source_replay, the new projection/optimization is consequential. Attribution against the unchanged source must include that shift; benefit cannot be ascribed to width allocation alone.\\\",\n      \\\"Failure of projection/compression equivalence, empty-history or padding invariance, parameter alias/optimizer audits, finite backward, or source gradient-gate tests invalidates the implementation and blocks substantive host training. Log the failed attempt and its cost; do not alter frozen inputs or contracts.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"alternative_explanations\\\": [\n      \\\"One training seed, changed initialization shapes and trainable projections can change optimization speed under the one-pass recipe; learned table rank and convergence are not separable from these observations alone. Same-seed source replay exactly reproduces AUC and is not an independent repetition.\\\",\n      \\\"Square projections are trainable rotations/scalings, not forward-identical controls for the original source. Their comparison to existing unprojected endpoints measures combined projection/optimization effects. No evidence here identifies redundancy of particular fields or frequency groups.\\\",\n      \\\"At fixed D, projection parameter counts differ by K*D*(16-8), even though nonlinear scorer/tower input sizes and hidden widths match. At fixed R, projection shape, dense input parameters, projection arithmetic and activation memory all vary with D. These are part of the allocated-capacity intervention, not a strict parameter-matched architecture contest.\\\",\n      \\\"R16,D8 still has an effective rank-eight linear map and cannot independently exploit all sixteen raw coordinates downstream; it is an overparameterized factorization control, not proof of higher effective representation rank. R8,D16 likewise has at most rank eight despite sixteen output coordinates.\\\",\n      \\\"Bias-free projection commutes with masked averaging in exact arithmetic; BF16 accumulation/casting can create small numeric differences. Host equivalence checks must distinguish tolerance-sized differences from operator errors.\\\",\n      \\\"Many small field projections, non-contiguous splits and concatenations can erase savings. Source inference wall time varied 24.46 to 26.72 seconds on an identical replay although model p50 was stable; loading time and accelerator noise can explain throughput changes.\\\",\n      \\\"Aliased embedding modules preserve shared projections, but cross-source sharing can let auxiliary context gradients reach a shared item table/projection. Keep source computational path gates and audit ownership; no exclusive semantic ownership claim follows from a detach.\\\",\n      \\\"All evidence is validation-only on the frozen released offline history policy, including potentially immature delayed feedback. No deployment-valid point-in-time claim, original-method reproduction claim, or verified priority claim.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"contrasts\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"table8_interact16 versus table8_interact8: lift the same raw table width 8 into 16 rather than 8 interaction coordinates.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"table8_interact8 is a new square-projection control; use g1-r0006-embedding_half to contextualize the effect of adding that projection.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"Raw table width and vocabulary/sharing\\\", \\\"All source inputs, masks, compression and gradient gates\\\", \\\"Scorer hidden 64/32 and tower hidden 128/64\\\", \\\"Frozen training exposure, seed, scoring and timing definitions\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Projection parameter/input dimension and nonlinear input-layer capacity change\\\", \\\"Different downstream initialization shapes and optimization\\\", \\\"No independent seed repetition in this phase\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"If the lift recovers AUC and the joint storage/latency thresholds hold against the unchanged source, retain it as a preliminary candidate and reserve paired host repetitions plus attribution against square16 and the source.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Report a failed interaction-width rescue; use the other factorial contrasts to determine whether table rank or projection cost is the more consequential limitation.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"table16_interact8 versus table16_interact16: narrow downstream coordinates while preserving raw table storage width.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"table16_interact16 is a new square-projection control. Existing g1-r0006-source_replay supplies the unchanged source, not another random initialization.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"Raw table width and lookup identities\\\", \\\"Same projection family and per-table alias policy\\\", \\\"Source pooling/gradient routing and hidden layer widths\\\", \\\"Frozen information, loss and host recipe\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Effective rank, projection shape and nonlinear input capacity vary\\\", \\\"Table16-interact8 may reduce latency without materially reducing total parameters\\\", \\\"Changed initialization and finite precision\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"Treat retained quality plus faster execution as support for downstream compression in this factorization, then seek a separately controlled storage reduction; do not claim the original joint goal is met from this cell alone.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Retain evidence that narrowing downstream coordinates is consequential in this tested factorization; do not infer that all history compression or interaction replacement is ineffective.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"At fixed D16 compare table8_interact16 against table16_interact16; at fixed D8 compare table8_interact8 against table16_interact8. Report the difference of these storage effects.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"Complete 2x2 projection factorial; bridge its square endpoints to existing g1-r0006-source_replay and g1-r0006-embedding_half. Existing g1-r0006-dense_half and g1-r0006-both_half are prior negative/interaction trajectories, not width-matched controls for this intervention.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"At each D, same nonlinear scorer/tower architecture\\\", \\\"Projection treatment present in every cell\\\", \\\"Source information flow and loss\\\", \\\"Training data passes and host scoring\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Raw table and projection initialization shapes\\\", \\\"Small extra projection parameter difference at fixed D\\\", \\\"Single-seed conditional effects; no causal claim about individual field redundancy\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"Localize whether retaining downstream coordinates attenuates the cost of halving table storage. Compare practical quality-cost frontiers with all original trials and preserve adverse auxiliary results.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Record null/negative factorial evidence and keep the unchanged source incumbent. Next falsifiable question: can a predeclared field-specific allocation, justified by authorized training-frequency diagnostics and a matched-storage control, retain quality? Do not choose fields from unseen or unavailable diagnostics.\\\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"cost_plan\\\": {\n      \\\"estimate_ref\\\": \\\"run://r-001 protocol estimated_unit_seconds=481.3475877419114, trial_cap_seconds=1203.3689693547785, remaining_seconds=157456.50017642975 at resolution. Relevant measured full units: g1-r0006-source_replay 303.4386s, embedding_half 277.7766s, dense_half 300.4170s, both_half 283.0406s. Budget is wall clock; source inspection, proposal preparation, checks and failed lookup attempts also consume it. No training is authorized in this propose phase.\\\",\n      \\\"all_variants_counted\\\": true,\n      \\\"attribution_reserve\\\": \\\"Four new full-protocol host cells, including both controls, are counted: nominal 1925.39s using the protocol estimate, conservative combined trial caps 4813.48s. Include prerequisite checks and failed trials. Reserve a further 6000s for authorized follow-up attribution and paired repetitions of a selected candidate, its closest square control and unchanged source (target three paired seeds when a later host interface permits them). This proposal never sets or changes a frozen training seed. Exact source replay is consistency evidence only. Projected cells may cost more despite fewer parameters; stop each at the unchanged host cap.\\\",\n      \\\"assessment_reserve\\\": \\\"Keep at least 6000s separate for eventual source/config/checkpoint freeze, closest references and key ablations, host-authorized final repetitions and closed assessment. No test request or test feedback in this phase; freeze the full comparison suite before any held-out evaluation. Withheld results remain in the closed archive and cannot enter open memory. Reserve is a planning floor, not permission to use another execution interface.\\\",\n      \\\"stop_rule\\\": \\\"Stop if user stop/hard deadline applies, host prerequisites or integrity fail, or no full admissible experiment fits while retaining the reserves. Do not raise any hard limit, duplicate an unknown-state job, install dependencies or run local training. Submit implemented modules and prospective plan only; host executes authorized checks/training. After host feedback, reject unsupported efficiency claims and preserve negative outcomes.\\\"\n    }\n  },\n  \\\"variants\\\": [\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table8_interact16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table8_interact16.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"candidate\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Primary table-storage reduction with learned 8-to-16 interaction lift. Compare to square8 and square16; success requires retention and measured cost against unchanged source. Source/config must be hashed before host execution; no local training.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table16_interact8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table16_interact8.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"candidate\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Replacement diagnostic: retain raw table storage, project to 8 interaction coordinates. Tests downstream compression under identical source hidden widths; alone cannot achieve large parameter saving.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table8_interact8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table8_interact8.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Square-projection compact control. Contrast with g1-r0006-embedding_half to expose projection/optimization effects; it is not an unchanged replay.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table16_interact16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table16_interact16.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Square-projection full-width control. Contrast with g1-r0006-source_replay to expose projection/optimization effects and record concurrent model timing. Existing source remains the quality/efficiency anchor.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge_assessments\\\": [\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-zenith\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"considered\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Earlier uniform reductions failed to preserve click AUC, justifying further allocation diagnostics. Available observations do not identify per-ID or per-field redundancy or frequency support, so do not expand IDs or adopt Zenith tokens. The primary-paper record is link-only; audited benchmark section is limited evidence.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None adopted from Zenith. All fields receive the same table width and projection-width policy.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Uniform storage-to-interaction maps under the compressed DIN source, rather than separate ID expansion and token interaction paths. No priority claim.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"If uniform factorization remains inadequate, selective capacity could be reconsidered only with authorized diagnostics and matched-storage controls.\\\"},\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-est\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"rejected\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Feature-specific FFNs and repeated sequence cross-attention would change the source mechanism and cost beyond this table/interaction attribution. Rejection is study-specific; no negative EST transfer has been measured.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None: the bias-free maps only change embedding coordinates; no cross-attention or feature-specific nonlinear FFNs are added.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Retain one action-aware compressed DIN readout; benchmark EST uses cross-attention and feature-specific FFNs. Original EST paper remains unaudited.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"Failure of all tested storage/interaction configurations would motivate a separately controlled interaction replacement, without establishing that EST would work.\\\"},\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-ssr\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"rejected\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Retrieved competitive sparse filtering does not directly separate table storage from interaction coordinates and may not produce actual speedups. No observed activation redundancy supports selecting this operator now.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None: no competitive filtering, learned sparsity or multi-view fusion.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Dense linear projection before the inherited scorer differs from benchmark SSR's sparse filtering after target pooling. Original SSR paper is not audited and no general novelty claim follows.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"A later measured redundancy diagnosis could justify sparse-versus-dense controls at matched capacity and cost; current results do not test SSR.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"host_prerequisites\\\": [\n    \\\"Verify original candidate.py/baseline_reference.py hashes against imported receipts and verify frozen data/protocol identities using the host's accepted readiness records. Raw parquet and torch are unavailable in this coding context; do not claim local data verification or execution.\\\",\n    \\\"For each module, instantiate on the actual FeatureMap; reject unexpected encoders/width overrides. Audit all expected fields, unique table/projection aliases, exact parameter counts and optimizer assignment: nn.Embedding to frozen Adagrad, dense projection/scorer/towers to frozen AdamW. Confirm all parameters exist before optimizer construction and host placement includes projections.\\\",\n    \\\"Run finite forward/backward with all four [B,1] probabilities and binary loss under the frozen precision. Test empty history, nonempty mixed feedback, all slots empty in individual blocks, and perturbations of masked historical item/action fields. Target action/current labels must not affect predictions; supplied task masks remain required.\\\",\n    \\\"Compare projected-after-compression and projected-before-compression outputs and gradients with identical parameters, masks and counts; use FP32 tight tolerance then the host's documented BF16 tolerance. No model redesign or contract change to pass the gate.\\\",\n    \\\"Audit source computational detach paths for projections as well as tables: auxiliary-only loss must not update item/action projections through blocked item uses or scorer parameters; context projection path remains active. Record alias-mediated overlap explicitly. Check Dice persistent buffers update only through the primary scorer call and eval uses one scorer pass.\\\",\n    \\\"Run all four full-protocol validation trials through the host only after prerequisites pass. Retain all receipts and failures. Same-seed endpoint comparisons are preliminary; do not substitute them for paired-seed/cluster uncertainty or leak held-out results.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"local_validation\\\": {\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"syntax_and_source_only\\\",\n    \\\"checks\\\": [\\\"Four modules parse with ast and compile without import/execution\\\", \\\"Literal CONFIG values match declared variants\\\", \\\"Only allowed model imports and no filesystem/network operations introduced\\\", \\\"Source diff reviewed; source compression, scorer calls, pooling, path gates and prediction heads retained\\\"],\n    \\\"limitations\\\": \\\"No torch installation, tensor execution, training, scoring, data digest validation or measured new-model cost. Authorized base_model reference lookup was unavailable; no attempt was made to inspect runtime internals. The shell diff command was unavailable; review used Python difflib.\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"memory_updates\\\": [\n    {\\\"maturity\\\": \\\"local_observation\\\", \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-dense_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"], \\\"record\\\": \\\"Append through authorized host receipt/memory storage: all tested uniform and hidden-width reductions lost source click AUC. Interaction between E and hidden widths changes sign across levels at one seed; this is not proof of redundant components. Source replay reproduces the same quality exactly while timing varies. No prior explanation is erased.\\\"},\n    {\\\"maturity\\\": \\\"hypothesis\\\", \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"], \\\"record\\\": \\\"Prospective revision: separate raw table width from nonlinear interaction width with a projection-treated factorial. This is untested. Do not record any projection benefit or held-out outcome in open memory before admissible validation evidence; human-owned and read-only memory files remain untouched.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /workspace/proposal.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"parent_trial\\\": \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n  \\\"study\\\": {\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"g1-capacity-storage-interaction-factorial\\\",\n    \\\"protocol_ref\\\": \\\"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\\\",\n    \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"baseline-din\\\", \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-dense_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"],\n    \\\"question\\\": \\\"Does the loss from uniform width reduction arise primarily from embedding-table rank/storage, from the dimension presented to the nonlinear scorer and towers, or from their interaction? Can an 8-dimensional table with a learned lift to 16 interaction coordinates retain the stronger source click AUC with fewer parameters and lower measured prediction cost?\\\",\n    \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Observed limitation: uniform E8 simultaneously reduced table width, target/history/context coordinates, the coordinate-product interaction and tower input widths. It saved about half the parameters but lost 0.00286509 click AUC. Dense-half lost 0.00117365 AUC with little parameter saving; applying dense-half at E8 instead increased AUC by 0.00041215 relative to embedding_half, an exploratory interaction of +0.00158580. These single-seed results do not locate redundant capacity. Provisional mechanism: some of the E8 loss may reflect the restricted geometry and input capacity of the nonlinear interaction rather than table rank alone. Separate raw table width R from downstream field width D through learned bias-free field projections, and test all four R,D in {8,16}. An R8,D16 lift remains rank at most eight per table; it cannot recreate an unrestricted 16-dimensional lookup. Its possible benefit is a learned interaction basis and wider nonlinear readout, not restored information. This is a diagnostic hypothesis, not demonstrated redundancy or a new-architecture claim.\\\",\n    \\\"nearest_work\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"trial://g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"implementation_checked\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Closest executable architecture: action-aware unnormalized DIN scorer over 30 masked uniform/feedback block summaries, four towers, auxiliary scorer/item gradient blocking with context gradients retained. Preserve all these operators and hidden widths; add a shared-by-table bias-free projection to decouple stored width from interaction width. Existing g1-r0006 factorial varied uniform embedding width and hidden widths, whereas this factorial holds hidden widths fixed and separates table width from downstream input width.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"paper:din\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"read\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Archived exact-version primary text inspected at lines 175-274: field embedding concatenation, target-dependent local activation, explicit product interactions and unnormalized pooling are inherited ideas. The local source adds block compression, four tasks and path gates. This proposal studies table/interaction width separation inside that source; no exact original DIN reproduction or novelty is claimed.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/embeddings/feature_embedding.py\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"implementation_checked\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Pinned implementation inspected at lines 55-200. Retain FeatureEmbeddingDict and its lookup sharing, padding and registered nn.Embedding modules. Add learned dense field projections after embedding/compression. Alias projections when their actual embedding modules are identical. Do not modify the host FeatureMap or vocabularies. Reject unexpected field dimension overrides/encoders rather than silently changing information.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"unirank-benchmark-v2\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"read\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Primary benchmark section 2.3 describes Zenith's separate ID paths, EST's cross-attention/feature-specific FFNs and SSR's sparse competitive filtering. None of these architectures is implemented here. The change is uniform table-to-interaction projection under an unchanged compressed source. Benchmark descriptions are not original-method full-paper audits.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"source_ref\\\": \\\"paper:zenith\\\",\n        \\\"verification\\\": \\\"discovered\\\",\n        \\\"difference\\\": \\\"Authorized record provides a primary-paper link and provenance only, with content_read=false. No original-method mechanism verification or priority comparison is asserted. The authorized paper search did not furnish an audited primary source for factorized recommendation embeddings; broader nearest-work coverage and originality remain unverified.\\\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"inherited_components\\\": [\n      \\\"Frozen data identity, official_offline visibility, four labels, supplied context/item/action fields, 100-event masks and temporal split.\\\",\n      \\\"g2-r0004-context_only source and its exact 10 blocks x 3 masked mean summaries, count weighting and uniform-click/feedback-auxiliary routing.\\\",\n      \\\"Action-aware unnormalized shared local activation with Dice and hidden widths 64/32; four separate towers with hidden widths 128/64.\\\",\n      \\\"Auxiliary functional scorer with detached parameters and cloned Dice buffers; item/action path detached for auxiliaries; context path trainable; single scorer call during inference.\\\",\n      \\\"Default sum of four unweighted BCEs; frozen single-pass host recipe, seed, optimizers, batch size, precision and scorers. No training-loss hook.\\\",\n      \\\"Framework embedding lookup and shared target/history tables, with all source fields retained.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"proposed_difference\\\": \\\"Four standalone cells independently set raw table width R and downstream per-field width D to 8 or 16. Every cell, including both square controls, adds one trainable bias-free R-to-D field map per unique underlying embedding module. Projections are initialized with orthogonal weights and gain sqrt(max(1,D/R)), after the source reset; this preserves average output-coordinate variance only for isotropic independent inputs. Raw histories are compressed before projection; linearity makes this equivalent in exact arithmetic to projecting each history before masked averaging. Current target and context use the same per-field maps; target/history aliases remain tied. Hidden scorer/tower widths and source gradient gates are unchanged. R8,D16 is the primary candidate; R16,D8 is a diagnostic replacement candidate, not expected to halve storage. R8,D8 and R16,D16 control for the added projection operator. Each module supplies a literal CONFIG and Model with the frozen prediction API. No new forward inputs, field removal, loss weights, data passes or optimizer changes.\\\",\n    \\\"predictions\\\": [\n      \\\"Primary diagnostic: if nonlinear interaction width matters beyond table rank, AUC(table8_interact16) exceeds AUC(table8_interact8), with a smaller gap between table8_interact16 and table16_interact16 than between the two square cells. Compare the difference of D effects across R to measure interaction, without presuming its sign.\\\",\n      \\\"If raw table rank is the dominant limitation, table8_interact16 remains below table16_interact16 despite identical downstream input and hidden widths. If compact downstream geometry is sufficient, table16_interact8 retains AUC relative to table16_interact16, isolating a possible latency reduction without a large storage benefit.\\\",\n      \\\"Operational screening retention is click AUC at least 0.660146940486458 (source 0.660646940486458 minus a predeclared 0.0005 margin), total parameters at least 40% below 32060453, and both model-only p50/p95 latency at least 5% below source replay 11.77057/11.90825 ms. Report whole-validation throughput separately; prefer a concurrent host timing control if authorized. These screening thresholds are not a confidence interval or established noninferiority. A joint efficiency claim needs repeated quality and timing support.\\\",\n      \\\"Embedding parameters should equal 15896608 at R8 or 31793216 at R16 if the original sharing/schema audit passes. With K unique projection owners, total counts should be 16048645+64K (R8,D8), 16163845+128K (R8,D16), 31945253+128K (R16,D8), and 32060453+256K (R16,D16). K and actual counts must be measured by the host. These are storage arithmetic predictions, not latency predictions.\\\",\n      \\\"Report all four AUC/logloss pairs, auxiliary mean separately, train/allocated-GPU/wall seconds, examples processed, peak memory, parameter split, validation inference seconds, throughput and p50/p95 batch latency. Source cart/fav/buy AUCs already trail baseline-din substantially; retaining click AUC must never be reported as retaining all-task quality. Use only existing history-length slice rules and show positives/negatives; slices and cross-cell effects remain exploratory until repeated.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"falsifiers\\\": [\n      \\\"No advantage of R8,D16 over R8,D8, together with a persistent gap to R16,D16, rejects the tested interaction-width rescue; it does not refute every mixed-width or low-rank design.\\\",\n      \\\"Neither R8 cell reaches the predeclared source-retention margin, or retention fails in later paired repetitions: no supported claim of preserving the stronger source at half table storage.\\\",\n      \\\"A compact-table cell that retains AUC but does not improve measured latency/throughput fails the joint prediction-cost claim. Parameter savings or FLOP estimates alone are insufficient.\\\",\n      \\\"If R16,D16 materially shifts quality relative to g1-r0006-source_replay, the new projection/optimization is consequential. Attribution against the unchanged source must include that shift; benefit cannot be ascribed to width allocation alone.\\\",\n      \\\"Failure of projection/compression equivalence, empty-history or padding invariance, parameter alias/optimizer audits, finite backward, or source gradient-gate tests invalidates the implementation and blocks substantive host training. Log the failed attempt and its cost; do not alter frozen inputs or contracts.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"alternative_explanations\\\": [\n      \\\"One training seed, changed initialization shapes and trainable projections can change optimization speed under the one-pass recipe; learned table rank and convergence are not separable from these observations alone. Same-seed source replay exactly reproduces AUC and is not an independent repetition.\\\",\n      \\\"Square projections are trainable rotations/scalings, not forward-identical controls for the original source. Their comparison to existing unprojected endpoints measures combined projection/optimization effects. No evidence here identifies redundancy of particular fields or frequency groups.\\\",\n      \\\"At fixed D, projection parameter counts differ by K*D*(16-8), even though nonlinear scorer/tower input sizes and hidden widths match. At fixed R, projection shape, dense input parameters, projection arithmetic and activation memory all vary with D. These are part of the allocated-capacity intervention, not a strict parameter-matched architecture contest.\\\",\n      \\\"R16,D8 still has an effective rank-eight linear map and cannot independently exploit all sixteen raw coordinates downstream; it is an overparameterized factorization control, not proof of higher effective representation rank. R8,D16 likewise has at most rank eight despite sixteen output coordinates.\\\",\n      \\\"Bias-free projection commutes with masked averaging in exact arithmetic; BF16 accumulation/casting can create small numeric differences. Host equivalence checks must distinguish tolerance-sized differences from operator errors.\\\",\n      \\\"Many small field projections, non-contiguous splits and concatenations can erase savings. Source inference wall time varied 24.46 to 26.72 seconds on an identical replay although model p50 was stable; loading time and accelerator noise can explain throughput changes.\\\",\n      \\\"Aliased embedding modules preserve shared projections, but cross-source sharing can let auxiliary context gradients reach a shared item table/projection. Keep source computational path gates and audit ownership; no exclusive semantic ownership claim follows from a detach.\\\",\n      \\\"All evidence is validation-only on the frozen released offline history policy, including potentially immature delayed feedback. No deployment-valid point-in-time claim, original-method reproduction claim, or verified priority claim.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"contrasts\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"table8_interact16 versus table8_interact8: lift the same raw table width 8 into 16 rather than 8 interaction coordinates.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"table8_interact8 is a new square-projection control; use g1-r0006-embedding_half to contextualize the effect of adding that projection.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"Raw table width and vocabulary/sharing\\\", \\\"All source inputs, masks, compression and gradient gates\\\", \\\"Scorer hidden 64/32 and tower hidden 128/64\\\", \\\"Frozen training exposure, seed, scoring and timing definitions\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Projection parameter/input dimension and nonlinear input-layer capacity change\\\", \\\"Different downstream initialization shapes and optimization\\\", \\\"No independent seed repetition in this phase\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"If the lift recovers AUC and the joint storage/latency thresholds hold against the unchanged source, retain it as a preliminary candidate and reserve paired host repetitions plus attribution against square16 and the source.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Report a failed interaction-width rescue; use the other factorial contrasts to determine whether table rank or projection cost is the more consequential limitation.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g2-r0004-context_only\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"table16_interact8 versus table16_interact16: narrow downstream coordinates while preserving raw table storage width.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"table16_interact16 is a new square-projection control. Existing g1-r0006-source_replay supplies the unchanged source, not another random initialization.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"Raw table width and lookup identities\\\", \\\"Same projection family and per-table alias policy\\\", \\\"Source pooling/gradient routing and hidden layer widths\\\", \\\"Frozen information, loss and host recipe\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Effective rank, projection shape and nonlinear input capacity vary\\\", \\\"Table16-interact8 may reduce latency without materially reducing total parameters\\\", \\\"Changed initialization and finite precision\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"Treat retained quality plus faster execution as support for downstream compression in this factorization, then seek a separately controlled storage reduction; do not claim the original joint goal is met from this cell alone.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Retain evidence that narrowing downstream coordinates is consequential in this tested factorization; do not infer that all history compression or interaction replacement is ineffective.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\",\n        \\\"intervention\\\": \\\"At fixed D16 compare table8_interact16 against table16_interact16; at fixed D8 compare table8_interact8 against table16_interact8. Report the difference of these storage effects.\\\",\n        \\\"control\\\": \\\"Complete 2x2 projection factorial; bridge its square endpoints to existing g1-r0006-source_replay and g1-r0006-embedding_half. Existing g1-r0006-dense_half and g1-r0006-both_half are prior negative/interaction trajectories, not width-matched controls for this intervention.\\\",\n        \\\"held_fixed\\\": [\\\"At each D, same nonlinear scorer/tower architecture\\\", \\\"Projection treatment present in every cell\\\", \\\"Source information flow and loss\\\", \\\"Training data passes and host scoring\\\"],\n        \\\"remaining_confounds\\\": [\\\"Raw table and projection initialization shapes\\\", \\\"Small extra projection parameter difference at fixed D\\\", \\\"Single-seed conditional effects; no causal claim about individual field redundancy\\\"],\n        \\\"decision_if_supported\\\": \\\"Localize whether retaining downstream coordinates attenuates the cost of halving table storage. Compare practical quality-cost frontiers with all original trials and preserve adverse auxiliary results.\\\",\n        \\\"decision_if_not_supported\\\": \\\"Record null/negative factorial evidence and keep the unchanged source incumbent. Next falsifiable question: can a predeclared field-specific allocation, justified by authorized training-frequency diagnostics and a matched-storage control, retain quality? Do not choose fields from unseen or unavailable diagnostics.\\\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \\\"cost_plan\\\": {\n      \\\"estimate_ref\\\": \\\"run://r-001 protocol estimated_unit_seconds=481.3475877419114, trial_cap_seconds=1203.3689693547785, remaining_seconds=157456.50017642975 at resolution. Relevant measured full units: g1-r0006-source_replay 303.4386s, embedding_half 277.7766s, dense_half 300.4170s, both_half 283.0406s. Budget is wall clock; source inspection, proposal preparation, checks and failed lookup attempts also consume it. No training is authorized in this propose phase.\\\",\n      \\\"all_variants_counted\\\": true,\n      \\\"attribution_reserve\\\": \\\"Four new full-protocol host cells, including both controls, are counted: nominal 1925.39s using the protocol estimate, conservative combined trial caps 4813.48s. Include prerequisite checks and failed trials. Reserve a further 6000s for authorized follow-up attribution and paired repetitions of a selected candidate, its closest square control and unchanged source (target three paired seeds when a later host interface permits them). This proposal never sets or changes a frozen training seed. Exact source replay is consistency evidence only. Projected cells may cost more despite fewer parameters; stop each at the unchanged host cap.\\\",\n      \\\"assessment_reserve\\\": \\\"Keep at least 6000s separate for eventual source/config/checkpoint freeze, closest references and key ablations, host-authorized final repetitions and closed assessment. No test request or test feedback in this phase; freeze the full comparison suite before any held-out evaluation. Withheld results remain in the closed archive and cannot enter open memory. Reserve is a planning floor, not permission to use another execution interface.\\\",\n      \\\"stop_rule\\\": \\\"Stop if user stop/hard deadline applies, host prerequisites or integrity fail, or no full admissible experiment fits while retaining the reserves. Do not raise any hard limit, duplicate an unknown-state job, install dependencies or run local training. Submit implemented modules and prospective plan only; host executes authorized checks/training. After host feedback, reject unsupported efficiency claims and preserve negative outcomes.\\\"\n    }\n  },\n  \\\"variants\\\": [\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table8_interact16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table8_interact16.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"candidate\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Primary table-storage reduction with learned 8-to-16 interaction lift. Compare to square8 and square16; success requires retention and measured cost against unchanged source. Source/config must be hashed before host execution; no local training.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table16_interact8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table16_interact8.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"candidate\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Replacement diagnostic: retain raw table storage, project to 8 interaction coordinates. Tests downstream compression under identical source hidden widths; alone cannot achieve large parameter saving.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table8_interact8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table8_interact8.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 8, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Square-projection compact control. Contrast with g1-r0006-embedding_half to expose projection/optimization effects; it is not an unchanged replay.\\\"},\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"table16_interact16\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"table16_interact16.py\\\", \\\"role\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"config\\\": {\\\"embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"table_embedding_dim\\\": 16, \\\"attention_hidden_units\\\": [64,32], \\\"tower_hidden_units\\\": [128,64], \\\"attention_normalization\\\": \\\"none\\\", \\\"compression_routes\\\": \\\"uf\\\", \\\"block_aux_scorer_grad\\\": true, \\\"block_aux_context_grad\\\": false, \\\"block_aux_item_grad\\\": true}, \\\"note\\\": \\\"Square-projection full-width control. Contrast with g1-r0006-source_replay to expose projection/optimization effects and record concurrent model timing. Existing source remains the quality/efficiency anchor.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge_assessments\\\": [\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-zenith\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"considered\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Earlier uniform reductions failed to preserve click AUC, justifying further allocation diagnostics. Available observations do not identify per-ID or per-field redundancy or frequency support, so do not expand IDs or adopt Zenith tokens. The primary-paper record is link-only; audited benchmark section is limited evidence.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None adopted from Zenith. All fields receive the same table width and projection-width policy.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Uniform storage-to-interaction maps under the compressed DIN source, rather than separate ID expansion and token interaction paths. No priority claim.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"If uniform factorization remains inadequate, selective capacity could be reconsidered only with authorized diagnostics and matched-storage controls.\\\"},\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-est\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"rejected\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Feature-specific FFNs and repeated sequence cross-attention would change the source mechanism and cost beyond this table/interaction attribution. Rejection is study-specific; no negative EST transfer has been measured.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None: the bias-free maps only change embedding coordinates; no cross-attention or feature-specific nonlinear FFNs are added.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Retain one action-aware compressed DIN readout; benchmark EST uses cross-attention and feature-specific FFNs. Original EST paper remains unaudited.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"Failure of all tested storage/interaction configurations would motivate a separately controlled interaction replacement, without establishing that EST would work.\\\"},\n    {\\\"knowledge_id\\\": \\\"unirank-method-ssr\\\", \\\"decision\\\": \\\"rejected\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Retrieved competitive sparse filtering does not directly separate table storage from interaction coordinates and may not produce actual speedups. No observed activation redundancy supports selecting this operator now.\\\", \\\"transformed_mechanism\\\": \\\"None: no competitive filtering, learned sparsity or multi-view fusion.\\\", \\\"variant_names\\\": [], \\\"nearest_work_difference\\\": \\\"Dense linear projection before the inherited scorer differs from benchmark SSR's sparse filtering after target pooling. Original SSR paper is not audited and no general novelty claim follows.\\\", \\\"falsifier\\\": \\\"A later measured redundancy diagnosis could justify sparse-versus-dense controls at matched capacity and cost; current results do not test SSR.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"host_prerequisites\\\": [\n    \\\"Verify original candidate.py/baseline_reference.py hashes against imported receipts and verify frozen data/protocol identities using the host's accepted readiness records. Raw parquet and torch are unavailable in this coding context; do not claim local data verification or execution.\\\",\n    \\\"For each module, instantiate on the actual FeatureMap; reject unexpected encoders/width overrides. Audit all expected fields, unique table/projection aliases, exact parameter counts and optimizer assignment: nn.Embedding to frozen Adagrad, dense projection/scorer/towers to frozen AdamW. Confirm all parameters exist before optimizer construction and host placement includes projections.\\\",\n    \\\"Run finite forward/backward with all four [B,1] probabilities and binary loss under the frozen precision. Test empty history, nonempty mixed feedback, all slots empty in individual blocks, and perturbations of masked historical item/action fields. Target action/current labels must not affect predictions; supplied task masks remain required.\\\",\n    \\\"Compare projected-after-compression and projected-before-compression outputs and gradients with identical parameters, masks and counts; use FP32 tight tolerance then the host's documented BF16 tolerance. No model redesign or contract change to pass the gate.\\\",\n    \\\"Audit source computational detach paths for projections as well as tables: auxiliary-only loss must not update item/action projections through blocked item uses or scorer parameters; context projection path remains active. Record alias-mediated overlap explicitly. Check Dice persistent buffers update only through the primary scorer call and eval uses one scorer pass.\\\",\n    \\\"Run all four full-protocol validation trials through the host only after prerequisites pass. Retain all receipts and failures. Same-seed endpoint comparisons are preliminary; do not substitute them for paired-seed/cluster uncertainty or leak held-out results.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"local_validation\\\": {\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"syntax_and_source_only\\\",\n    \\\"checks\\\": [\\\"Four modules parse with ast and compile without import/execution\\\", \\\"Literal CONFIG values match declared variants\\\", \\\"Only allowed model imports and no filesystem/network operations introduced\\\", \\\"Source diff reviewed; source compression, scorer calls, pooling, path gates and prediction heads retained\\\"],\n    \\\"limitations\\\": \\\"No torch installation, tensor execution, training, scoring, data digest validation or measured new-model cost. Authorized base_model reference lookup was unavailable; no attempt was made to inspect runtime internals. The shell diff command was unavailable; review used Python difflib.\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"memory_updates\\\": [\n    {\\\"maturity\\\": \\\"local_observation\\\", \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"g1-r0006-source_replay\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-dense_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"], \\\"record\\\": \\\"Append through authorized host receipt/memory storage: all tested uniform and hidden-width reductions lost source click AUC. Interaction between E and hidden widths changes sign across levels at one seed; this is not proof of redundant components. Source replay reproduces the same quality exactly while timing varies. No prior explanation is erased.\\\"},\n    {\\\"maturity\\\": \\\"hypothesis\\\", \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"g1-r0006-embedding_half\\\", \\\"g1-r0006-both_half\\\"], \\\"record\\\": \\\"Prospective revision: separate raw table width from nonlinear interaction width with a projection-treated factorial. This is untested. Do not record any projection benefit or held-out outcome in open memory before admissible validation evidence; human-owned and read-only memory files remain untouched.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
